    "q-71402": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71402",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=9x+3y-4$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n\nII. $c=-4$ gives a line\n\nIII. $c=5$ gives a hyperbola",
      "worked_solution": "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x+3y-4 & =c \\\\ 3y & =-9x+c+4 \\\\ y & =-3x+\\frac{c+4}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=-3x+\\frac{4}{9},$ which is not an ellipse.\n\n- If $c=-4$ then the level curve is $y=-3x,$ which is a line.\n\n- If $c=5$ then the level curve is $y=-3x+3,$ which is not a hyperbola.\n\nSo, only statement II is true.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
